  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced`, but I didn't rename the old fields. All 39 tests pass.\n\nARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event. A straight rename would break them as soon as it deployed, and the rule says renames go through deprecation. So `totalCents` and `placedAt` are still published with the same values, marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`. I left `schemaVersion` at 3 because the change is additive. I updated `test/app.test.ts` to check both the new and the old fields.\n\nI didn't touch the `GET /orders/{id}` response (`src/api/responses.ts`). It still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`, and web-storefront depends on it (ARCH-8). I also left the internal `Order.placedAt` as it is.\n\nTo finish the rename, check that billing-service and analytics-ingest read the new fields. Then remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` from the event, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can add a removal date to the deprecation comments if you tell me the agreed timeline.",
